7-05/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Vinquoy Chambered Cairn is a chambered cairn (tomb) on Eday, Orkney, Scotland (central claim) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinquoy_chambered_cairn]; It stands on the highest point of Eday, above Calf Sound [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinquoy_chambered_cairn]; It is built of red sandstone [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinquoy_chambered_cairn]; It has a 5 m passage leading to a central chamber [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinquoy_chambered_cairn]; The central chamber has four small side-cells [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinquoy_chambered_cairn]; The cairn is carved into the hill [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vinquoy_chambered_cairn]"}]'::jsonb),
