", "quote": "The Valley of the Temples is an archaeological site at Agrigento (central claim) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; The site is in Italy (Agrigento, Sicily) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; It is not a valley (the name is a misnomer) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; It is in fact a ridge [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; The ridge lies outside Agrigento [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; It holds the remains of seven temples [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; The seven temples are Doric [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; The Temple of Concordia is among them [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]; The Temple of Concordia was once clad in polychrome stucco [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valle_dei_Templi]"}]'::jsonb),
